    "reconstructionNotes": "RCE primary description substantiates ten cast-iron fluted columns with composite capitals, open decorated friezes, railings, nine stone steps and a shallow overhanging timber tent roof with onion finial. Roof plan is the exact OSM decagon; basement/column circle sits within it. DSM peak minus nearby DTM median is 7.7805 m; a restrained 8 m finial allows thin-detail sampling uncertainty. Ornamental shapes and individual vertical proportions are low-poly visual approximations. No solid wall fills the pavilion; surrounding island and wooden bridge remain existing park geometry."
